+# Routed execution
+
+Owns complete generic, stereo, and home-cinema routed execution, preprocessing,
+crossover training, splice rollback, and routing result assembly. Shared native
+playback, acceptance, seat identity, and resource computations live in playback.
+
+Five explicit application operations retain actual channel/supporting-source
+resource ownership, MSO/DBA source adapters, and prepared system execution in
+workflow. This avoids normal and dev dependencies from routed to workflow or
+sibling channel/system/finalization coordinators. Arguments and callback delivery
+are preserved; workflow supplies the existing implementations, including retries,
+receipt identity, recovery and sidecar persistence.
+
+All166 existing topology cases remain workflow integration tests in their
+original namespaces. No tests are replaced with mocks. Workflow unit adapters
+pass the same assembly reference and inject the real application operations;
+assembly fields and borrowing lifetimes remain unchanged. The test-support
+feature exposes internal topology helpers only for these existing integration
+contracts. The library creates no empty unit-test harness.
+
+This is a full source-only extraction prototype. It is not accepted or ported.
+Graph/feature/privacy checks, exact native scope, compilation, strict Clippy,
+waveform/receipt/rollback behavior, domain QA, coverage and paired performance
+measurements are required. Include the costs of shared prerequisites and public
+interfaces in marginal and combined accept/reject decisions.
